<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea sets new stock trading range from Nov 25.</title>
<headline>S.Korea sets new stock trading range from Nov 25.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea will allow stock prices to fluctuate within eight percent on either side of the previous close from November 25, the Korea Stock Exchange said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The price movement band is currently set at six percent.  </p>
<p>The trading band would be further widened to 10 percent in 1997, an exchange statement said.</p>
<p>It said the looser fluctuation limit would allow the bourse to more quickly reflect market conditions and was part of the exchange's drive to liberalise market regulations.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
